  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public investment programs include specific activities to enhance risk prevention and mitigation as a result of the implementation of the 2010#2014 Development Plan.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2011-02-28" value="0% of all investments" year="2011">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2011-02-28"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2014-08-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Public investment programs include an investment on specific activities to enhance risk prevention and mitigation as a result ofthe implementation of the 2010-2014 Development Plan"></target>
     <actual value="1. During the first semester of 2014, MARN was assigned a total amount of $4.1 million as part of loans from CABEI and allocationsfrom the national budget to enhance DRM.
2. Betweem 2009 and 2014, MINSAL invested more than $306 million in hospitalinfrastructureand equipment, including construction of 5 new hospitals and reconstruction/remodeling of several health centers.
3.During 2009-2014, MINED invested more than $95.6 million in rehabilitation and/or construction of schools,  repairs of storm damageas well as mitigation measures."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public investment programs include specific activities to enhance risk prevention and mitigation as a result of the implementation of the 2010#2014 Development Plan.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2011-02-28" value="0% of all investments" year="2011">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2011-02-28"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2014-08-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Public investment programs include an investment on specific activities to enhance risk prevention and mitigation as a result ofthe implementation of the 2010-2014 Development Plan"></target>
     <actual value="1. MARN was assigned an additional amount of $3,418,209 as part of loans from CABEI and allocations from the national budget toenhance DRM.
2. MINSAL invested more than $183 million to build two new hospitals and to reconstruct 16 other health centers inaccordance with the PAHO hospital safety index.
3. In 2013, MOP finalized projects in the amount of $16.7 million to addressemergencies inthe transport sector (bridges and roads) and build mitigation measures.
4. Overall, STP allocated$25 million to thevarious ministries to cope with the impact of Tropical Depression 12E. In October 2013, two megashelters that were built with thesefunds were inaugurated."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consistent with 2010#2014 Development Plan, key ministries have included risk analysis initiatives in their development plans, leading to a better use of technical information on natural disasters to</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2011-02-28" value="1 ministry" year="2011">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2011-02-28"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2014-08-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Consistent with 2010-2014 Development Plan, at least three key ministries have included risk analysis initiatives in theirdevelopment plans, leading to a better use of technical information on natural disasters to refine and guide investment programs toreduce vulnerability."></target>
     <actual value="1. MARN conducted 9 stakeholder workshops at various levels as part of the consultation process for the First National ClimateChange Plan; advanced the development of the three action plans under the National Environmental Strategy taking into account DRMconsiderations; carried out 20 more training days for municipal staff, as well as 3 regional workshops and 1 national workshop topromote risk monitoring and adequate use of early warning systems; developed a 2014-2018 institutional strategy based oncomprehensive DRM and climate change adaptation; and has advanced in vulnerability assessment for groundwater bodies to defineaction guidelines.
2. MINSAL continued the assessment of health centers using the PAHO hospital safety index and will haveevaluated 100% of national hospitals by the second semester of 2014; 61% of the 28 hospitals that have been evaluated thus farcomply with the safety requirements, 36% need assistance, and 3% need immediate intervention, for the latter categories improvementplans have been elaborated; MINSAL also evaluated 223 Community Health Centers.
3. MINED has finalized the geo-referencing ofschools and assessing their general vulnerability to flooding and landslides using the School Safety Index (548 schools are exposedto landslides, 289 to flooding); as part of a CAPRA project, detailed seismic vulnerability analysis of 65 schools was conductedand their emergency plans were reviewed; MINSALalso continued to provide DRM capacity building to teachers, pupils and communityleaders.
4. MOP put together an inventory of public infrastructure that is vulnerable to earthquakes, including prioritizationand costs of necessary mitigation action, and has initiated the implementation of the prioritized mitigation actions; completed theFlood Assessment Plan for Urban Drainage; and has further advanced the development of a vulnerability assessment methodology forpublic infrastructure 
5. STP conducted trainings for damage assessment and management of community shelters."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consistent with 2010#2014 Development Plan, key ministries have included risk analysis initiatives in their development plans, leading to a better use of technical information on natural disasters to</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2011-02-28" value="1 ministry" year="2011">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2011-02-28"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2014-08-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Consistent with 2010-2014 Development Plan, at least three key ministries have included risk analysis initiatives in theirdevelopment plans, leading to a better use of technical information on natural disasters to refine and guide investment programs toreduce vulnerability."></target>
     <actual value="1. MARN installed real--time monitoring equipment in 8 additional municipalities (total of 88 municipalities) and carried out 12more training days; initiated consultation processes to elaborate the Action Plans for the four strategic pillars of the newNational Environmental Strategy; approved guidelines for environmental zoning and land use planning that incorporate DRMconsiderations for 28 municipalities (including San Salvador); launched a capacity building program for DRM and Climate Change inOCtober 2013 and carried out a workshop on mitigation of geo-risks in August 2013; has further advanced in risk assessment andmapping for flood and seismic risk prone areas.
2. MINSAL continued the assessment of health centers using the PAHO hospital safetyindex and, to date, has evaluated 93% of national hospitals; also continued to update the emergency plans of hospitals;
3. MINEDhas geo-referenced 6035 schools (including 923 private schools) and provided DRM capacity building to 500 schools;
4. MOP hascontinued to incorporate DRM considerations into public investment projects; carried out over 65 risk and damage assessmentsrelated to landslides and flooding and 30 topograhic surveys; prepared several manuals for damage and vulnerability assessment ofpublic infrastructure and bridges; and conducted trainings on search and rescue in disaster situations."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The GoES is better prepared to respond to adverse natural events and Sectoral Emergency Response Plans and other Plans are implemented in relevant situations.</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2011-02-28" value="Civil Protection and Disaster Prevention and Mitigation National Plan updated in July 2009; seven Sectoral Emergency ResponseCommissions approval by the National Commission on October, 5, 2009; seven Sectoral Emergency Response Plans submitted for approvalby the National Commission on November 30, 2010; National Earthquake Contingency Plan approved by the National Commission onOctober, 5, 2009; and 2010 Rainy Season Plan approval by the National Commission on May 7, 2010." year="2011">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2011-02-28"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2014-08-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Sectoral Emergency Response Plans and other Plans are in force and implemented in relevant situations."></target>
     <actual value="1. The National Plan for Civil Protection has been strengthened by finalizing the incorporation of guidelines for rehabilitationand reconstruction and the inclusion of additional risks to have an integral vision of DRM.
2. The National Commission is in theprocess of adopting the proposal for the National Policy for Civil Protection and Disaster Prevention.
3. The 7 Sectoral EmergencyResponse Commissions continue to meet regularly, and in 2014 contingency plans for floods, seismic activity and epidemics (dengue)were activated.
4. The National Seismic Contingency Plan for earthquakes and tsunamis was tested through a simulation in May 2014with the support of the Humanitarian Allied Forces (FAHUM) and the participation of the sectoral commissions.
